```
Reason: After `usb_alloc_urb()` successfully allocates a URB, if `usb_submit_urb()` fails, the function returns immediately without calling `usb_free_urb()`, causing a memory leak of the allocated URB.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
	ret = usb_submit_urb(usbio->urb, GFP_KERNEL);
	if (ret) {
		dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Submitting usb urb\n");
		goto err_free_urb;
	}

...

err_free_urb:
	usb_free_urb(usbio->urb);
	return ret;
```
Reason: By jumping to `err_free_urb` after a submission failure, the URB is always freed via `usb_free_urb()`, eliminating the memory leak. The new label also correctly handles any other errors that may occur later in the function, ensuring the URB is freed when those paths are taken (e.g., after `err_unlock`).

